  <body>
    <div class="example" id="string-interpolation">
      <h2><a href="./">F# by Example</a>: String Interpolation</h2>
      
      <table>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            
          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            <a href="https://try.fsharp.org/#?code=UmQF_oO4Nk-"><img title="Run code" src="play.png" class="run" /></a><img title="Copy code" src="clipboard.png" class="copy" />
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="k">open</span> <span class="nn">System</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            
          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="k">let</span> <span class="nv">name</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="s">&#34;John&#34;</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            <p>String interpolation is prefixed with <code>$</code>
values that you want to inject in the string are templated with curly braces <code>{}</code></p>

          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="k">let</span> <span class="nv">a</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="o">$</span><span class="s">&#34;Hello, {name}&#34;</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            <p>Anything inside the <code>{}</code> can be treated as a valid expression
This means you can do more expressive stuff inside</p>

          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="k">let</span> <span class="nv">b</span> <span class="o">=</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">    <span class="o">$</span><span class="s">&#34;&#34;&#34;Hello, 
</span></span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="s">    {if name &lt;&gt; &#34;John&#34; then name else &#34;[redacted]&#34;}&#34;&#34;&#34;</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            
          </td>
          <td class="code leading">
            
          <pre class="chroma"><code><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="n">printfn</span> <span class="s">&#34;%s&#34;</span> <span class="n">a</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="n">printfn</span> <span class="s">&#34;%s&#34;</span> <span class="n">b</span></span></span></code></pre>
          </td>
        </tr>
        
        <tr>
          <td class="docs">
            <p>Note: If you want to reference string literals within string interpolation
expression you should wrap the whole string with triple quotation marks</p>

          </td>
          <td class="code empty">
            
          
          </td>
        </tr>
        
